cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "SageGUI: a graphical interface for the Sage proteomics search engine"
abstract: >-
  A desktop graphical interface for the Sage proteomics search engine. It
  configures and runs a Sage search without the command line: mzML and FASTA
  selection, enzyme and tolerance settings, modifications, and TMT or LFQ
  quantification. Sage is compiled in, so a search runs in the same process as
  the interface. Bundled templates and a reader for Sage config.json and
  results.json files reproduce a known search configuration.
type: software
version: 0.8.0
date-released: "2026-09-09"
authors:
  - family-names: Neely
    given-names: Benjamin A.
    affiliation: "National Institute of Standards and Technology"
    email: benjamin.neely@nist.gov
# A DOI goes here when one is minted. Add a top-level `doi:` key at this
# level; nothing else has to change. An empty or placeholder value fails
# CFF validation, so the key is left out until a real DOI exists.
repository-code: "https://github.com/neely/sagegui"
url: "https://github.com/neely/sagegui"
# `license-url:` and not `license:`. The NIST Software Licensing Statement has
# no SPDX identifier, and `license:` only accepts SPDX values.
license-url: "https://github.com/neely/sagegui/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - proteomics
  - mass spectrometry
  - database search
  - graphical user interface
  - peptide identification
